    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="letterhead">FRIENDS CONFERENCE ON NATURE AND LAWS
                        <lb/>OF OUR SPIRITUAL LIFE <lb/>ASSOCIATED WITH THE <lb/>AMERICAN FRIENDS
                        FELLOWSHIP COUNCIL</fw><fw place="left" type="letterhead">20 South 12th
                        Street <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__747" type="place">Philadelphia</rs>
                        7, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__998" type="place">Penna.</rs></fw><fw
                        place="right" type="letterhead">TELEPHONE <lb/>RITTENHOUSE
                            9372</fw><dateline><date when="1946-04-09">April 9/46</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr.
                        Tillich</rs>,</salute></opener>
                <p>I have just received the enclosed letter from a member of committee of above
                    conference, &amp; as I understand it was through you that <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__3470" type="person">Dr. Elkisch</rs> entered the N.
                    Y. psych group, I am taking the liberty of asking you for any pertinent
                    information you may have to give us about her. What is her training &amp;
                    background? I<pb n="2"/> was told at first that
                    she<!-- evtl. was/is supplien --> a Jungian analyst, &amp; then again that she
                    was not. As you know, we remain somehow very anonymous to each other in that
                    psych. group, &amp; one has to glean information about one&apos;s fellow-members in
                    roundabout ways. (It is one of the things I have a real concern to do something
                    about incidentally, for I can see it is hampering our real effectiveness).</p>
                <p>How would <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3470" type="person">Dr. Elkisch</rs> be as
                    a discussion leader in a conference group, where most people know <hi rend="u"
                        >something</hi> of psychology, but not too much?<pb n="3"/></p>
                <p>If you could let me have the main facts as soon as possible I should be grateful,
                    &amp; perhaps I could see you <unclear>next</unclear> time I am in <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs> for further
                    elucidation. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1084" type="person">Walter</rs> has
                    just got home, &amp; we shall both be in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319"
                        type="place">N. Y.</rs> I think the last weekend of this month, as the
                    psych. group meets on the <date when="1946-04-26">26<hi rend="sup"
                        >th</hi></date> (Friday) &amp; <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1084"
                        type="person">Walter</rs> has <del rend="s">a</del> meetings from the <date
                        when="1946-04-28">28<hi rend="sup">th</hi></date> on. You will be glad to
                    hear that he was able to visit his parents &amp; sister<pb n="4"/> in <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__776" type="place">Austria</rs> before coming home
                    – he spent 9 days in travel for 24 hours there!</p>
                <p>Please give my kindest regards to <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1923"
                        type="person">Mrs. Tillich</rs>. I wish she &amp; you would attend the group
                    again – it has come <hi rend="u">much</hi> more alive this winter. In fact so
                    much dynamite has been touched that it has looked as if the group might
                    evaporate in smoke occasionally – but we have re-crystallized each time so
                    far!</p>
                <closer><salute>Sincerely yours,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3469"
                            type="person">Elined Prys</rs></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
